<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Butilin</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 554</span> · Also known as Buccelin</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Butilin, or Buccelin, was an Alemannic duke in the service of the Frankish Merovingian kings. With his brother <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/leuthari">Leuthari</a> he led a large Frankish and Alemannic army into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a> in 553 during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gothic-war-535-554">Gothic War</a>, raiding as far south as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/campania">Campania</a>. In 554 the Byzantine general <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/narses">Narses</a> destroyed his army, already weakened by disease, at the Battle of the Volturnus, and Butilin was killed.</p></div>
